From: mscharged-port
Subject: Diagnostic: the rollback's log names the disc reads the game starts
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Rollback study, after tweak patch 0029. A rollback cannot go back across a
disc read into the game's memory: a network match whose steps started one
on predicted inputs that then turned out wrong desyncs (a captain's super
ability, the play after a kickoff). Which reads those are, and where the
match is when the game starts them, is what a way through them needs.

nlOpen tells the rollback the path and entry number of every file it opens
(mscharged_rollback_file_opened), and nlReadAsync every read it starts, with
the file's entry number and where the bytes go
(mscharged_rollback_read_started), files opened before included. While the
rollback tracks a match its log names each read with the frame, the task
running, whether the frame is a first run or a replay and whether inputs
are still predicted; a rollback a read stops lists the writes under way and
the files they come from.

Without RECHARGED_ROLLBACK_TEST or RECHARGED_ROLLBACK, or a log, nothing
changes.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_rollback.h b/include/mscharged_rollback.h
--- a/include/mscharged_rollback.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_rollback.h
@@ -46,6 +46,13 @@
 // after it was undone. Outside tracked steps, everything goes out.
 bool mscharged_rollback_determ_data_new(int frame, const void* data, unsigned size);
 #endif
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+// The disc reads, for the log while the rollback tracks a match (a rollback
